  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian political landscape is currently addressing the vacancy in the vice presidency following the resignation of Gibran Rakabuming Raka. According to constitutional procedures, President Prabowo Subianto has a two-week period to propose two candidates to the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR). The MPR is tasked with facilitating the selection through a plenary session, with leadership now coordinating the necessary scheduling and procedural steps. As consultations between the President and coalition leaders continue, public discussion regarding potential successors has intensified. Different political entities have maintained varied positions; for example, the Democratic Party has officially announced it will not propose any names, while other groups have identified their preferred candidates. Organizations like Al Washliyah have urged national unity during this transition, emphasizing the need for the future Vice President to focus on navigating significant economic challenges alongside the President.",
